  "summary": "Tallahassee city commissioners will again discuss the city's use of ALPRs, including 80 Flock and 75 Vigilant cameras, after Gov. DeSantis ordered such cameras off state roadways. A prior motion by Commissioner Jeremy Matlow to end the Flock contract failed 3-2; Police Chief Lawrence Revell defended the cameras, citing their role in solving violent crimes and a new transparency portal showing 1,300+ searches last month.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "At the last meeting, Commissioner Jeremy Matlow made a motion to end the city's contract with Flock, citing privacy concerns. That motion failed 3 to 2.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "The report continues that the camera data can be kept up to 30 days and audited regularly for inappropriate use.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "This is back on the city's agenda after Gov. Ron DeSantis ordered the cameras removed from state roadways.",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    }
  ],
